WEBVTT

00:00:08.935 --> 00:00:10.562
(roaring)

00:00:10.645 --> 00:00:13.523
Where is he? When I am through
with that one-eyed weasel

00:00:13.607 --> 00:00:15.525
he's going to need two eye patches.

00:00:17.319 --> 00:00:19.696
I admire your bloodthirstitude, Gertie.

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:20.947
But you heard them.

00:00:21.031 --> 00:00:23.033
An asteroid is coming.

00:00:23.116 --> 00:00:25.869
(laughs) This changes things.

00:00:27.495 --> 00:00:28.538
(yelps)

00:00:28.622 --> 00:00:30.916
Holy snowballs! It's freezing up here.

00:00:30.999 --> 00:00:33.293
Parts are retracting
into other parts. (screams)

00:00:33.376 --> 00:00:35.795
Would you please
stop acting like a parakeet?

00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:38.715
It's a good thing
you got your mother's eyes

00:00:38.798 --> 00:00:40.592
or you'd be totally useless.

00:00:40.675 --> 00:00:42.344
Well, that's just hurtful. (screams)

00:00:44.638 --> 00:00:45.931
-(neck cracks)
-(screams)

00:00:46.014 --> 00:00:47.224
What do you see?

00:00:48.141 --> 00:00:50.852
-(sighs) Nothing. Nothing.
-(screaming)

00:00:51.519 --> 00:00:53.688
Deadly asteroid screaming towards Earth.

00:00:54.522 --> 00:00:56.399
Wait! There he is.

00:00:56.483 --> 00:00:59.444
That's too bad. He is really far away.

00:00:59.527 --> 00:01:01.238
Probably too far to reach by flight.

00:01:01.321 --> 00:01:02.572
Oh, well. Let's just go home.

00:01:03.156 --> 00:01:04.991
We are not retreating!

00:01:05.075 --> 00:01:06.910
Until that weasel came along

00:01:06.993 --> 00:01:09.079
our family made an honest living

00:01:09.162 --> 00:01:10.413
stealing dino eggs.

00:01:10.497 --> 00:01:12.791
An honest living. Stealing.

00:01:12.874 --> 00:01:14.251
Kind of ironic, don't you think?

00:01:14.668 --> 00:01:16.920
Besides, why take out the weasel

00:01:17.003 --> 00:01:18.922
if the asteroid is just gonna take us out?

00:01:19.005 --> 00:01:21.591
So much sight. So little vision.

00:01:21.675 --> 00:01:24.010
If we stop the weasel and his friends

00:01:24.094 --> 00:01:25.845
from diverting the asteroid...

00:01:25.929 --> 00:01:26.930
Kablooie!

00:01:27.013 --> 00:01:29.641
It kills the weasel and everyone else,

00:01:29.724 --> 00:01:33.645
while we glide safely above it all.

00:01:33.728 --> 00:01:36.439
It'll be our paradise.

00:01:36.523 --> 00:01:37.774
(laughing evilly)

00:01:37.857 --> 00:01:40.110
That's seems highly implausible.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:41.987
Just from a scientific standpoint.

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:43.113
(both growl)

00:01:43.196 --> 00:01:45.865
Fine. It's a great plan. Dynamite!

00:01:45.949 --> 00:01:48.952
One of the top three or four
species annihilation plans I've ever heard.

00:01:49.035 --> 00:01:50.453
That's better.

00:01:50.537 --> 00:01:54.207
Now let's make sure that asteroid hits.

00:01:54.749 --> 00:01:57.794
Why can't we just fear the apocalypse
like a normal family?

00:02:06.261 --> 00:02:07.304
(gasps)

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:09.931
(exclaims)

00:02:11.224 --> 00:02:12.976
(grunting)

00:02:17.564 --> 00:02:18.565
(exclaims)

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.193
(sniffs)

00:02:22.277 --> 00:02:23.278
Whoa!

00:02:24.237 --> 00:02:25.238
(sniffs)

00:02:26.614 --> 00:02:27.615
(screams)

00:02:29.659 --> 00:02:30.660
(gasps)

00:02:31.578 --> 00:02:32.579
Mmm.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.081
(screams)

00:02:38.251 --> 00:02:39.252
(screaming)

00:02:45.759 --> 00:02:46.760
Mmm?

00:02:47.344 --> 00:02:48.345
(screaming)

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.359
(panting)

00:03:02.442 --> 00:03:03.443
(gasps)

00:03:04.611 --> 00:03:05.779
(growling)

00:03:05.862 --> 00:03:06.863
(grunting)

00:03:09.699 --> 00:03:11.117
(screaming)

00:03:12.118 --> 00:03:13.578
(toilet flushing)

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.125
(screaming)

00:03:34.349 --> 00:03:35.350
(sniffing)

00:03:38.561 --> 00:03:39.896
What are you doing, Buck?

00:03:39.979 --> 00:03:41.815
All rocks tell a tale.

00:03:42.565 --> 00:03:45.568
Where we've been and where we're heading.

00:03:45.652 --> 00:03:46.611
-(sniffing)
-(both gasp)

00:03:46.694 --> 00:03:47.737
(both sniffing)

00:03:47.821 --> 00:03:49.406
Ah!

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:51.908
That, however, is a turd.

00:03:55.995 --> 00:03:57.163
Julian...

00:03:57.247 --> 00:04:00.458
I want you to know
that if we don't make it,

00:04:00.542 --> 00:04:02.752
if we never get married,

00:04:02.836 --> 00:04:04.462
you were the only one for me.

00:04:04.546 --> 00:04:06.673
Hey, come on!

00:04:06.756 --> 00:04:09.592
Of course we'll make it,
and we will get married.

00:04:09.676 --> 00:04:12.178
But maybe it's the universe
telling us we won't.

00:04:12.262 --> 00:04:13.471
SID: Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

00:04:13.555 --> 00:04:16.015
You're going to let one tiny little

00:04:16.099 --> 00:04:19.185
300-mile-wide asteroid ruin your plans?

00:04:19.269 --> 00:04:20.520
How can we think about our future

00:04:20.603 --> 00:04:22.021
when we may not have one?

00:04:22.105 --> 00:04:23.606
Hey, we're going to stop this thing

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:24.941
and you'll get married.

00:04:25.024 --> 00:04:26.943
Bada-bing, bada-boom!

00:04:27.026 --> 00:04:29.279
Well, not boom. Forget I said boom.

00:04:29.696 --> 00:04:30.697
(gasps)

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.199
I know! I'll be your wedding planner!

00:04:33.283 --> 00:04:36.494
It'll take your mind
off all this end-of-the-world stuff.

00:04:36.578 --> 00:04:39.038
Actually, we were just gonna wing it!

00:04:39.122 --> 00:04:40.123
(chuckles) Keep it low-key.

00:04:40.206 --> 00:04:41.708
What?

00:04:41.791 --> 00:04:43.460
Peaches, Peaches. Sweetheart,

00:04:43.543 --> 00:04:46.463
you don't just wing
the happiest day of your life!

00:04:46.546 --> 00:04:49.549
No, you seize it and you cherish it.

00:04:49.632 --> 00:04:52.051
You strangle it with good intentions.

00:04:53.052 --> 00:04:55.138
Ooh. Let's start with your hair.

00:04:56.055 --> 00:04:58.892
Updo with a top bun? Traditional.

00:04:58.975 --> 00:05:02.979
Or updo with a fishtail braid. Flirtatious.

00:05:03.062 --> 00:05:04.063
(giggling)

00:05:04.147 --> 00:05:06.232
But maybe a little trashy.

00:05:07.108 --> 00:05:08.485
Ugh.

00:05:08.568 --> 00:05:10.069
And garter belts!

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:13.323
Today, Ed is modeling laced daisies.

00:05:13.406 --> 00:05:15.825
While Crash is rocking a more elegant ivy

00:05:15.909 --> 00:05:17.911
that's all about the calves.

00:05:17.994 --> 00:05:19.704
Ooh. We need a seating chart!

00:05:19.787 --> 00:05:22.165
The singles table, the kids table,

00:05:22.248 --> 00:05:23.666
the weird relatives table,

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.628
the smelly table, two more smelly tables.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:28.505
(scoffs) Look at him.

00:05:28.588 --> 00:05:30.131
JULIAN: Oh, you're gonna love it.

00:05:30.215 --> 00:05:31.841
Who walks like that?

00:05:31.925 --> 00:05:33.843
(mimicking Julian) Oh! Look at me.

00:05:33.927 --> 00:05:35.136
I'm Julian.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.679
Forget the asteroid.

00:05:36.763 --> 00:05:38.973
Gimme a hug, Bro-Dad!

00:05:39.057 --> 00:05:41.476
(clears throat) Look at
that pretty bird there.

00:05:41.559 --> 00:05:42.560
(squawks)

00:05:43.269 --> 00:05:46.648
Yeah! That is a pretty bird.
Good eye, Manny.

00:05:46.731 --> 00:05:48.149
(chuckles) Yeah.

00:05:48.233 --> 00:05:49.567
The sky is literally falling

00:05:49.651 --> 00:05:50.985
and she thinks we're just gonna

00:05:51.069 --> 00:05:52.529
let her stroll into the wilderness

00:05:52.612 --> 00:05:54.531
with Mr. No Plans Bouncy Walk.

00:05:54.614 --> 00:05:56.157
Stop picking on him.

00:05:56.241 --> 00:05:59.035
Come on, El, you're not
still mad at me, are you?

00:05:59.118 --> 00:06:00.578
No. I'm not still mad.

00:06:00.662 --> 00:06:02.205
Because that's not how I want to spend

00:06:02.288 --> 00:06:03.915
what could be our final days together.

00:06:03.998 --> 00:06:07.544
But if we somehow survive
that planet-killing hunk of space rock,

00:06:07.627 --> 00:06:08.711
you're in for it.

00:06:08.795 --> 00:06:11.047
If we survive, we lose our daughter.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:13.091
Well, I've been thinking about that, too.

00:06:13.174 --> 00:06:14.676
What if...

00:06:14.759 --> 00:06:17.220
Ooh. I know! We destroy
the relationship, right?

00:06:17.303 --> 00:06:18.930
That way we never have to let her go

00:06:19.013 --> 00:06:21.849
and she'll just stay our little girl forever!

00:06:21.933 --> 00:06:23.560
(laughing)

00:06:23.643 --> 00:06:25.520
No, you psychopath!

00:06:25.603 --> 00:06:29.190
What if we convince them to stay near us?

00:06:29.274 --> 00:06:31.359
Oh! That's better.

00:06:31.442 --> 00:06:33.444
I like it. But how?

00:06:33.528 --> 00:06:35.613
The way we always
get her to do what we want.

00:06:35.697 --> 00:06:37.991
We make her think it's her idea.

00:06:38.366 --> 00:06:41.452
You sneaky, sneaky minx! (giggles)

00:06:41.536 --> 00:06:43.955
Let's just hope we haven't lost our touch.

00:06:44.038 --> 00:06:45.164
Found it!

00:06:46.332 --> 00:06:47.917
Behold, mammals!

00:06:48.001 --> 00:06:51.087
A sneak preview of the asteroid to come.

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:54.632
A space rock. Fresh from the cosmos.

00:06:55.216 --> 00:06:56.593
Mmm, mmm, mmm.

00:06:56.676 --> 00:06:58.803
I taste iron, carbon.

00:06:58.886 --> 00:06:59.929
(gargles)

00:07:00.013 --> 00:07:02.307
Oh! And a hint of nickel.

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:03.433
(sighs)

00:07:03.516 --> 00:07:05.393
Space tastes lonely.

00:07:05.476 --> 00:07:07.395
Hey, look! I found another one.

00:07:07.478 --> 00:07:08.479
Me, too!

00:07:08.896 --> 00:07:09.897
(both screaming)

00:07:13.985 --> 00:07:14.986
Hmm...

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:17.447
Hey! Yours is attracted to me.

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:20.116
No. Yours is attracted to me.

00:07:20.199 --> 00:07:22.076
(grunting and screaming)

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.161
(Eddie sobs)

00:07:23.244 --> 00:07:25.788
We're just too attractive!

00:07:25.872 --> 00:07:29.667
Stupendous! Now we have something
to play with during our final hours.

00:07:30.001 --> 00:07:31.628
You're missing the point, Tiger.

00:07:31.711 --> 00:07:33.004
They're magnets.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:36.132
And if these space rocks are magnetic,

00:07:36.215 --> 00:07:37.383
so is that.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:42.096
This can only mean one thing.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.057
And that would be...

00:07:44.932 --> 00:07:46.100
Allow me.

00:07:46.184 --> 00:07:47.185
(both scream)

00:07:48.394 --> 00:07:49.687
Whoa!

00:07:49.771 --> 00:07:51.105
Where are we?

00:07:51.189 --> 00:07:53.232
(echoing) You are in my brain.

